## Iteration 10 Complete

**Finding:** One P2 issue: the sk-code routing example uses a fixed `TASK` heredoc delimiter. If task text contains a line exactly equal to `TASK`, the shell ends stdin there and executes subsequent lines as commands. A safe shell probe confirmed the behavior. This conflicts with the changelog’s claim that the quoted heredoc keeps task text inert. [ROUTER.md](/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/sk-code/ROUTER.md:497) · [sk-doc changelog](/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/changelog/v2.10.1.0.md:21) · [compiled-route.cjs](/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs:34)

